     "page_section_element_title": [],
     "page_section_element_body": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "Consistent use of colour is a vital component of maintaining a cohesive and in-brand visual language. In the Aalto design system colours are mainly used on background surfaces to highlight important parts of a page or a screen. All actionable interface elements are neutral coloured, meaning white or shades of grey depending on the background they are placed on.",
       "spans": [],
       "direction": "ltr"
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "This page explains the colours as tokens in the design system. If you're interested in the colour usage from our brand perspective, visit the Colours page under Visual guidelines. ",
       "spans": [
        {
         "start": 142,
         "end": 149,
