     "page_section_element_body": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "Base palette includes all the colours of the system. These colours should not be used by directly copying the HEX value, but rather by using tokens to call for the correct colour. This is to reduce the strain of memorising values and to ensure accessibility of the final product, but will also make system wide colour changes easier.",
       "spans": [],
       "direction": "ltr"
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "There are five groups in the Base palette. These groups are ",
       "spans": [],
       "direction": "ltr"
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "- Aalto Brand: Colours and tints for Aalto's brand colors.\n- School: Colours and tints for Aalto's six schools.\n- Neutral: Greyscale colours that form the basis of any interface and interactive element.\n- Transparent: Transparent colours that are used to create states for interactive elements.\n- Tint: Solid colour alternatives to the Transparent group, intended for cases where semi-transparent layers cannot be used due to technical or other limitations.",
       "spans": [
        {
