   {
    "primary": {
     "type": "TextChapter",
     "page_section_element_title": [
      {
       "type": "heading6",
       "text": "",
       "spans": []
      }
     ],
     "page_section_element_body": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "Themes are colour collections that define the colours for light and dark modes as well as brand and school coloured elements. A theme defines the values for each usable colour to keep the system accessible.",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "A neutral theme, light or dark, is always the basis of a page or screen. On top of this sections can have their own themes. Different sections have different limitations on which themes can be used. For example, cards are always used with neutral themes. Obviously themes Light and Dark are never used in the same layout.",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "The leading thought is that bright colours from brand and school themes are used on sections that have important information and thus need to be highlighted.",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "There are a total of 12 themes which are divided into three groups. These groups are Neutral, Brand and School.",
       "spans": []
      }
     ],
     "component_id": null,
     "component_figma_link": {
      "link_type": "Any"
     },
