   {
    "primary": {
     "type": "TextChapter",
     "page_section_element_title": [
      {
       "type": "heading6",
       "text": "Action and Action reversed",
       "spans": []
      }
     ],
     "page_section_element_body": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "Action and Action reversed are used for all interactive elements. These groups are identical in logic, but one is dark and the other is light. Action group is the main action colour in every theme, whereas Action reversed is used when contrasting elements are needed inside these actions. ",
       "spans": [],
       "direction": "ltr"
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "For example, in the primary button the button background is filled with the Action colour and button label is filled with the Action Rev colour. Different states are built by adding a contrasting fill colour to the button background.",
       "spans": [],
       "direction": "ltr"
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "- Action is the default colour for interactions\n- Action Reversed is used for adding contrasting elements on top of the action colour\n- Hover or Hover Reversed is used to indicate a hovered state depending on the background colour of the element\n- Active or Active Reversed is used to indicate an active state depending on the background colour of the element\n- Disabled or Disabled Reversed is used for disabled elements\n- Selected or Selected Reversed is used to indicate a selected state depending on the background colour of the element",
       "spans": [
        {
         "start": 0,
         "end": 8,
         "type": "strong"
        },
        {
